00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:17.620
And it's a pretty simple--

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.460
it's actually pretty
much just a link.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.310
So if you've got
your code on GitHub

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.250
and it either uses a build
pack or it's dockerized,

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.380
then you can just take
this quick button, put it

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.243
into your GitHub
repo, and then people

00:02:28.243 --> 00:02:30.160
who are viewing that
repo can click the button

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.800
and it'll just send it
right over to Cloud Run.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.690
So you don't need to
do any additional work.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.990
It's just a really fantastic way
for someone to take your code

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.940
and be like, oh, well,
I can see the code,

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.340
