00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.060
I've got a fun one, too,
by a fellow teammate.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.380
Dane Zeke Liergaard
did an article

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.810
and has written a solution
for Firebase Unity

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.780
Solutions, Update game
behavior without deployment

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:14.800
with Remote Config.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.320
So Remote Config's a
great Firebase tool

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.120
can be used for mobile
apps, especially,

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.240
if you want to be able to
change how your app behaves

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:22.813
at runtime.

00:03:22.813 --> 00:03:24.730
Basically, you can change
configuration values

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:27.040
within the Firebase Console,
and that gets propagated out

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.690
to all your applications,
and you know,

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.330
you can be like, make this thing
bluer or redder, or et cetera.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.680
This is also great
for games, as well.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.930
Maybe you want to change
things like difficulty levels

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.550
or how many hit points are
available to certain characters

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.550
in the game, or if you
want to balance your play

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.530
style or your play
mechanics inside your game,

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.290
without having to push
a whole new versions.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:43.870
MARK MIRCHANDANI: Right.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.760
There's so much extra
work that has to go

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:46.907
into pushing a new version.

00:03:46.907 --> 00:03:47.740
But if you can use--

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:47.980
MARK MANDEL: Yep.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.430
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
--Remote Config,

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:50.597
it sounds like you're easily
able to just say, well,

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.870
let's make these tiny
tweaks, and then people

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.610
will see those changes
instantaneously.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:55.360
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.785
So what's super
nice about this is

00:03:56.785 --> 00:03:59.830
this is built in directly
into the Unity Editor.

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.350
You can just pop in the
provided component onto you

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.120
any game object
or prefab, and you

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:06.712
can tweak how you want
to basically set up

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:08.170
each of the properties
within there

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:11.080
and how they tie to the
Remote Config Management API.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.750
Not only that, once your
game is actually live,

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.790
you can actually go back
into the Unity Editor,

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.899
see the values that
are available in there,

00:04:17.899 --> 00:04:19.690
and actually upload
any changes you

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.578
want to try tweaking
locally up to Remove

00:04:21.578 --> 00:04:23.620
Config so it gets propagated
out without actually

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.703
having even to go to the
Firebase Console as well.

00:04:25.703 --> 00:04:26.590
So super nice thing.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.120
Thank you very much
for that work, Dane.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:28.510
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
